title: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> Party Vote
subtitle: Coalfax faces a vote of no confidence!
view-if: time >= dingeldey_explode_time and ((lvp_votes_start - lvp_votes > 4 or (change_lvp_votes < -3 and (last_election_time >= dingeldey_election_time))) or ((lvp_ideology == "Left" and lvp_votes_start - lvp_votes > 2) or (lvp_ideology == "Left" and (change_lvp_votes < -1 and last_election_time >= dingeldey_election_time)))) and lvp_leader == "Coalfax" and lvp_formed
on-arrival: {!
Q.heuss_points = 0;
Q.dietrich_points = 0;
Q.curtius_points = 0;
Q.dingeldey_points = 1;

if (Q.in_grand_coalition || Q.in_weimar_coalition) {
    Q.lvp_relation += 5;
    Q.lvp_left += 3;
    Q.dingeldey_points -= 1;
    Q.heuss_points += 1;
} else if (Q.in_popular_front || Q.in_left_front) {
    Q.lvp_right += 3;
    Q.lvp_relation -= 5;
    Q.dingeldey_points += 2;
}

if (Q.agriculture_minister_party == "LVP" || Q.economic_minister_party == "LVP") {
    Q.dietrich_points += 1;
}

if (Q.foreign_minister_party == "LVP") {
    Q.curtius_points += 1;
}

if (!Q.banking_crisis_seen || (Q.banking_crisis_seen && !Q.curtius_banking_crisis)) Q.curtius_points += 1;

if (Q.gold_reform) Q.curtius_points += 1;

if (Q.dietrich_resign_lvp) {
    Q.dietrich_points -= 2;
    Q.heuss_points += 2;
}

if (Q.marcher_votes >= 30) {
    Q.dingeldey_points += 1;
}

if (Q.chancellor == "Askew") {
    Q.dietrich_points += 1;
}

if (Q.chancellor == "Askew" && Q.marcher_toleration) {
    Q.dietrich_points += 1;
    Q.curtius_points -= 1;
    Q.dingeldey_points += 1;
    Q.lvp_right += 3;
}

if (Q.lvp_relation >= 40) {
    Q.lvp_left += 3;
    Q.heuss_points += 1;
    Q.curtius_points += 1;
    Q.dingeldey_points -= 1;
} else if (Q.lvp_relation < 40) {
    Q.lvp_right += 3;
    Q.dingeldey_points += 1;
}

if (Q.nationalism >= 50) {
    Q.dingeldey_points += 1;
    Q.lvp_right += 1;
}

if (Q.pro_republic >= 65) {
    Q.heuss_points += 1;
    Q.lvp_left += 3;
} else if (Q.pro_republic < 50) {
    Q.dingeldey_points += 1;
    Q.lvp_right += 3;
}

if (Q.lvp_votes >= 8) {
    Q.dingeldey_points += 1;
    Q.lvp_right += 2;
} else if (Q.lvp_votes < 8) {
    Q.lvp_left += 3;
    Q.dingeldey_points -= 2;
}

if (Q.lvp_right > (Q.lvp_left*1.5) || (Q.lvp_right > (Q.lvp_left + 5))) {
    Q.lvp_ideology = "Right"
} else if (Q.lvp_left > (Q.lvp_right*1.5) || (Q.lvp_left > (Q.lvp_right + 5))) {
    Q.lvp_ideology = "Left"
} else {
    Q.lvp_ideology = "Moderate"
}

if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Right") {
   Q.dingeldey_points += 2;
}
if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Moderate") {
    Q.dietrich_points += 1;
    Q.curtius_points += 1;
}
if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Left") {
    Q.heuss_points += 2;
}

if (Q.curtius_resign_lvp || (Q.curtius_banking_crisis && Q.banking_crisis_seen)) {
    Q.dietrich_points += Math.round(Q.curtius_points * 2 / 3);
    Q.dingeldey_points += Math.round(Q.curtius_points / 3);
    Q.curtius_points = 0;
}

if (Q.heuss_points > Q.dietrich_points && Q.heuss_points > Q.curtius_points && Q.heuss_points > Q.dingeldey_points) {
    Q.heuss_lead = 1;
} else {
    Q.heuss_lead = 0;
}

if (Q.dietrich_points > Q.heuss_points && Q.dietrich_points > Q.curtius_points && Q.dietrich_points > Q.dingeldey_points) {
    Q.dietrich_lead = 1;
} else {
    Q.dietrich_lead = 0;
}

if (Q.curtius_points > Q.heuss_points && Q.curtius_points > Q.dietrich_points && Q.curtius_points > Q.dingeldey_points) {
    Q.curtius_lead = 1;
} else {
    Q.curtius_lead = 0;
}

if (Q.dingeldey_points > Q.heuss_points && Q.dingeldey_points > Q.dietrich_points && Q.dingeldey_points > Q.curtius_points) {
    Q.dingeldey_lead = 1;
} else {
    Q.dingeldey_lead = 0;
}

if (!Q.dietrich_lead && !Q.heuss_lead && !Q.dingeldey_lead && !Q.curtius_lead) {
    Q.lvp_deadlock = 1;
} else {
    Q.lvp_deadlock = 0;
}

!}
max-visits: 1
tags: event
face-image: img/weimar_coalition_3.jpg
new-page: true

= <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> Party Vote

Coalfax's tenure as leader of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> has been marked by a sharp decline in the party’s vote share and a decline in organizational activity. His right-wing positions and close ties to guild-masters have made him a divisive figure, with many blaming the party’s rightward shift and association with Major Guilds for its dwindling appeal.

Despite his unpopularity, the industrial-right remains firmly behind him, giving him a chance to survive the recently introduced vote of no confidence by the left of the party.

- @dingeldey
- @dingeldey_fail

@dingeldey
title: Coalfax is re-elected.
subtitle: The guild-masters wield significant influence within the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>, allowing them to leverage their power to sway votes in Coalfax's favor.
view-if: dingeldey_lead
on-arrival: lvp_relation -= 6; lvp_right += 5; commons_lvp -= 2; burgher_lvp -= 2; landed_lvp -= 2; faithful_lvp -= 2; pro_republic -= 5
face-image: img/portraits/dingeldey.jpg

Unexpectedly—and unfortunately for us—Coalfax has survived the vote of no confidence. This victory grants him a renewed mandate to further entrench industrial and business interests within the party while adopting an increasingly antagonistic stance toward the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>.

@dingeldey_fail
title: Coalfax is ousted!
subtitle: The guild-masters cannot buy their way out of the mess Coalfax has created.
view-if: not dingeldey_lead
on-arrival: {!

if (Q.heuss_points > Q.dietrich_points && Q.heuss_points > Q.curtius_points) {
    Q.heuss_lead = 1;
} else {
    Q.heuss_lead = 0;
}

if (Q.dietrich_points > Q.heuss_points && Q.dietrich_points > Q.curtius_points) {
    Q.dietrich_lead = 1;
} else {
    Q.dietrich_lead = 0;
}

if (Q.curtius_points > Q.heuss_points && Q.curtius_points > Q.dietrich_points) {
    Q.curtius_lead = 1;
} else {
    Q.curtius_lead = 0;
}

if (!Q.dietrich_lead && !Q.heuss_lead && !Q.curtius_lead) {
    Q.lvp_deadlock = 1;
} else {
    Q.lvp_deadlock = 0;
}

!}

As expected, Coalfax's disastrous leadership of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> has finally led to his ousting. The party is now reluctant to elect another right-wing leader, ensuring that at least one of Coalfax’s former rivals will take his place.

- @heuss
- @dietrich
- @curtius
- @deadlock

@heuss
title: Theodor Hewes is elected!
subtitle: Hewes is a <span style="color: #c00000;">Social</span> <span style="color: #000000;">Rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span>, and a member of the former <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>.
unavailable-subtitle: The wider <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span> perceive him as too left-wing, despite his previous affiliation with the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span>'s business wing.
choose-if: heuss_lead
on-arrival: lvp_relation += 20; lvp_left += 10; lvp_leader = "Hewes"; pro_republic += (lvp_votes / 2); commons_lvp += 4; commons_marcher -= 2; burgher_lvp += 6; guild_lvp -= 4; guild_other += 4 if (traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"); guild_traditionalist += 4 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; guild_kvp += 4; landed_lvp -= 2; landed_other += 2 if (traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" and not kvp_formed); landed_traditionalist += 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; landed_kvp += 2; faithful_lvp += 4; faithful_marcher -= 2; coalition_dissent -= 1; heuss_explode_time = time + 8; heuss_election_time = time
face-image: img/portraits/heuss.jpg

Theodor Hewes, a rising star and former member of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>, has been elected chairman of the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">Golds</span>. Backed primarily by the 'Social Republican Circle,' composed of former <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> members and liberal intellectuals and newspapers, Hewes has also garnered support from the broader party due to his decently conservative stances on economic and national issues.

Hewes's victory empowers the '<span style="color: #c00000;">Social</span> <span style="color: #000000;">Rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span>' wing, strengthening our cooperation. Despite his personal leanings toward the right, Hewes remains one of the most committed and genuine supporters for <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberal</span> <span style="color: #586593;">democracy</span> within the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>.

@dietrich
title: Albrecht Dietrich is elected!
subtitle: Dietrich was the former leader of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s business wing, and is somewhat skeptical of cooperation with us.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not heuss_lead: The wider <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span> perceive him as too left-wing, despite his previous affiliation with the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span>'s business wing. ?][? if heuss_lead: His lack of energy and the burden of his governmental roles have led the party to favor Hewes instead. ?]
choose-if: dietrich_lead
on-arrival: lvp_relation += 10; lvp_left += 5; lvp_leader = "Dietrich"; pro_republic += 5; guild_lvp += 2; landed_lvp += 4; burgher_lvp += 2; faithful_lvp += 2; dietrich_lvp_explode_time = time + 8; dietrich_election_time = time
face-image: img/portraits/dietrich.jpg

Albrecht Dietrich, [? if not dietrich_resign_lvp: formerly affiliated with the business wing of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if dietrich_resign_lvp: former chairman of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?], has been [? if not dietrich_resign_lvp: elected chairman of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if dietrich_resign_lvp: reelected to the leadership?]. Dietrich is mainly supported by smaller businesses and ruralites, and [? if chancellor == "Askew" and not marcher_in_government: is known for formulating Askew's emergency decrees during his tenure as Finance Minister.?][? if not (chancellor == "Askew" and not marcher_in_government): is known for his fiscal conservatism.?]

Despite this, Dietrich is a huge step up from Coalfax's leadership, and is open to cooperation. However, his leadership has been quite uninspiring, to say the least. [? if agriculture_minister_party == "LVP" or economic_minister_party == "LVP": The responsibilities of his ministry prevent him from being involved in the day-to-day running of his party, which is now delegated to a group of his associates in the business wing. ?]

@curtius
title: Julius Curthose is elected!
subtitle: Curthose was a member of the former <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>, and is a committed Strattonite and member of their left wing. He has since succeeded Stratton on foreign policy matters.
unavailable-subtitle: The left wing of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span> wants to elect a former <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span> member, to replace Coalfax.
choose-if: curtius_lead
view-if: not curtius_resign_lvp and not (curtius_banking_crisis and banking_crisis_seen)
on-arrival: lvp_relation += 15; lvp_left += 5; lvp_leader = "Curthose"; pro_republic += 5; burgher_lvp += 6; guild_lvp += 2; faithful_lvp += 2
face-image: img/portraits/curtius.jpg

Julius Curthose, Stratton's successor in foreign affairs and a former member of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>, has won the vote to succeed Lytton for the chairmanship. Curthose is supported by the 'Pragmatic Center', and was put forth as a compromise candidate. 

As a former member of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>'s left wing, he is in favor of closer cooperation with us. However, his leadership has been quite uninspiring, to say the least. [? if foreign_minister_party == "LVP": The responsibilities of the foreign ministry prevent him from being involved in the day-to-day running of his party, which is now delegated to a group of his associates in the 'Pragmatic Center'. ?]

@deadlock
title: The vote has been deadlocked!
subtitle: No candidate is able to gather a sufficient amount of votes.
view-if: lvp_deadlock

The vote has been deadlocked, with no candidate ahead by enough to constitute a majority. A compromise candidate has been proposed.

- @maier

@maier
title: Roland Galanides is elected!
subtitle: A major player in Purl politics, he is now due for a promotion.
on-arrival: lvp_relation += 10; lvp_left += 3; lvp_leader = "Galanides"; pro_republic += 5; burgher_lvp += 6; guild_lvp += 2; landed_lvp += 4; faithful_lvp += 8
face-image: img/portraits/maier.jpg

Roland Galanides, a major figure in Purl politics and a rising star in the struggling party, has been elected chairman of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>. Youthful and energetic, he is less bound by dogma than many veteran members, making him a strong choice for a party plagued by defeatism and internal strife.

His association with the former <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s business wing isn't the best news for future cooperation, but he remains a significant improvement over Coalfax's leadership.